        "reviewText": "Validated by researcher · Ido Carmel · 2026-10-08\n\nValidation covers the model extraction and SPPR diagnostics in the signed report. Current calculation results and availability are assessed separately.\n\nModel extraction notes\n\nAccepted corrections: Chrysaora plocamia (7) diet is 68% mesozooplankton, 17% macrozooplankton and 15% anchovy eggs, with zero direct diatom/small-gelatinous links. Author Table H I14/J14 reconstructs the 68/17 fractions; F14/K14 are zero and Table B H39 retains the egg fraction. This resolves the contradictory Table B diet totaling 1.045 without changing small-gelatinous biomass.\n\nSardine (9) landings follow the article’s explicit 1.4 t/km2/year correction; reported discards 0.17462648325 remain. Total JSON export is 1.57462648325; estimated EE is recalculated to 0.68720654. Article Table 1 and Scenario III still support the older high-catch branch. These are documented reconstructions/derived corrections, not newly printed author values.\n\nThe corrected model passes mass balance with living BA=0 and normalization compensation disabled. GS retains source assimilation efficiencies. Runtime normalization of the remaining diets is separate; pool EE/BA and detritus-fate identity replacement remain computational transformations. Native fleet discard-return ancestry is unsupported in the SPPR translation.\n\nPublished-source extraction audit | Source conflicts | Prior loader matrix audit\n\nRetained departures and evidence limits:model notes\n\nGE diagnostics\n\nWARN: successful pooled-detritus GE result with EE floor 0.1 and det_collapse_mode='auto'.\n\nPooled groups 36–39: SPPR = 4.9871. No negative entries across any basal-source column or recipient. rho_living = 0.7000; PP budget check: OK.\n\nUnpooled option: FAIL (b = 1.6236 > 1). The saved engine aggregate grade remains FAIL because it carries the unpooled recycling check; it is distinct from the pooled-result WARN reported here. A current pooled b was not retained.\n\nSeabirds (31) remains near-singular. Both current methods retain an unexplained negative Benthic detritus (39) stock residual of −4337.3803. No missing source supply has been invented; budget closure does not establish ecological validity.\n\nCurrent GE full return\n\nHistorical reviewed entry and numerical comparison are retained in the EE floor calculation update at the end of this report.\n\nTE diagnostics\n\nWARN: EE-floor TE result. The PP budget check is now OK (gap = 0.0000077%); the historical result was FAIL with a 14% gap.\n\nNo negative SPPR entries across any basal-source column or recipient. rho_living = 0.7316.\n\nDetritus SPPR: Anchovy eggs (36) = 0.0000; Fishery offal (37) = 0.0000; Pelagic detritus (38) = 0.3050; Benthic detritus (39) = 0.0000.\n\nNear-singular groups remain: Cetaceans (33), Pinnipeds (32) and Seabirds (31). The negative detritus stock residual described above also remains. The five formerly EE=0 living groups and Chrysaora plocamia now have effective EE = 0.1; their source values are unchanged.\n\nSettings retain use_ee_floor=True, ee_floor=0.1, det_collapse_mode='auto' and fix_EE_0_cases=True. TE does not pool in this run. Its b = 0 denotes no detritus recycling matrix, rather than evidence of ecological validity.\n\nCurrent TE full return\n\nHistorical reviewed entry and numerical comparison are retained in the EE floor calculation update at the end of this report.\n\nSPPR Calculation Notes\n\nValidation applies only when collapse_det_mode='auto' is used for all SPPR_new-related calculations (calculator keyword: det_collapse_mode='auto'). Engine diagnostic grades remain unchanged.\n\nRemoved groups from calculations:\n\nFishery offal (EE=0)\n\nPinnipeds (GE<1.0%, EE=0)\n\nSeabirds (GE<0.10%, EE=0)\n\nChrysaora plocamia (EE near-zero)\n\nGeographic fit\n\nApproximate A. Region covered by study: 6.0–8.0%.\nApproximate B. Study covered by region: 90–100%. The northern shelf domain leaves most of this LME outside the model